我想是叫这个，或者神秘山，我记不清了。

00:11:54.750 --> 00:11:56.169
But it's on YouTube, you can watch it now.
但它在YouTube上，你现在就能看。

00:11:56.169 --> 00:11:58.129
It's got hundreds of thousands of views.
它有几十万的播放量。

00:11:58.129 --> 00:11:59.450
It's so funny.
太搞笑了。

00:11:59.450 --> 00:12:05.009
It's like a Parks and Rec meets office kind of mockumentary about these park rangers.
这有点像《公园与游憩》遇上《办公室》那种关于公园管理员的伪纪录片。

00:12:05.009 --> 00:12:07.690
And they got picked up by a studio.
而且他们被一家制片厂看中了。

00:12:07.690 --> 00:12:14.450
They're making more of them now because they're from Nashville, you know?
他们现在正在拍更多集，因为他们来自纳什维尔，你知道吗？

00:12:14.450 --> 00:12:17.370
And now they're living in Los Angeles making a TV show.
现在他们住在洛杉矶拍电视剧。

00:12:17.370 --> 00:12:19.809
So just make stuff.
所以尽管去创作吧。

00:12:19.809 --> 00:12:39.830
Yeah, I feel like when what interests you is film or television, there does feel like this huge gulf between you and the ability to make the art you want to make, which is so different from being a singer-songwriter with your guitar on your stool or a painter.
是的，我觉得当你的兴趣是电影或电视时，你确实会觉得你和创作你想制作的艺术之间存在一条巨大的鸿沟，这和那些抱着吉他坐在高脚凳上的唱作人或者画家截然不同。

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:51.070
And yeah, I mean the joy of gathering up your friends of gathering up your friends in the bar and saying, I'm going to make this thing.
是的，我是说，把你的朋友们聚集在酒吧里，说“我要拍这个东西”，这种感觉本身就是一种快乐。

00:12:51.070 --> 00:13:12.190
And it's hard, there's something hard inside you that goes, but wait a second, this isn't a real movie because this studio that's owned by a company that makes washing machines is not making my movie, so it's not real, there are an advertisement up on Billboard, so it's not real.
这很难，你内心深处会有某种声音在说：“但等一下，这不是一部真正的电影，因为这家被制造洗衣机的公司所拥有的制片厂没有拍我的电影，所以它不是真的，也没有在巨型广告牌上打广告，所以它不是真的。”

00:13:12.190 --> 00:13:19.870
And that's an internal thing I've had to get over and people have to get over to say, no, no, I made a movie from start to finish.
这是我不得不克服的内心障碍，也是大家必须克服的心理，我们要对自己说：“不，不，我从头到尾制作了一部电影。”

00:13:19.870 --> 00:13:20.909
That's a movie.
这就是一部电影。

00:13:20.909 --> 00:13:24.070
I can't really control one outcome.
我无法真正控制某一种结果。

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:29.629
If there's something about, it's a screen and it literally feels like a screen, like how do you get in there?
如果有什么特别之处，那就是它是一个屏幕，而且感觉真像是一个屏幕，比如你怎么才能进到里面去？

00:13:29.629 --> 00:13:30.990
How do you get into that screen?
你怎么才能进到那个屏幕里？

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:35.669
It feels like so far, like the golf, the chasm.
感觉太远了，就像那条沟壑，那道深渊。

00:13:35.669 --> 00:13:44.669
Whereas if you go to the theater, you go see stand up, you go see a musician, There are a couple feet from you, maybe, depending on how good your ticket is.
然而如果你去剧院，去看脱口秀，去看音乐演出，他们离你只有几英尺远，也许吧，这取决于你的票有多好。

00:13:44.669 --> 00:13:54.629
And you can see like, oh, they're up on stage and I know that's hard to get up, but it almost feels easier than a screen to navigate that or get there.
你可以看到，哦，他们就在舞台上，我知道要站上去不容易，但比起银幕，要克服这种距离或到达那里，感觉似乎更容易一些。

00:13:55.710 --> 00:14:00.710
But there's no substitution for doing it and failing.
但动手去做并经历失败是无可替代的。

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:06.750
I actually heard Quentin Tarantino, big how I made your mother fan, Quentin Tarantino, not a lot of people know this.
我其实听说昆汀·塔伦蒂诺——很多人不知道这一点——其实是个《老爸老妈浪漫史》的超级大粉丝。

00:14:06.750 --> 00:14:13.309
And I don't think this is apocryphal, maybe can someone can fact check this, but that he actually directed a movie before Reservoir Dogs.
而且我觉得这并非道听途说，也许有人可以核实一下，他在《落水狗》之前其实导演过一部电影。

00:14:13.309 --> 00:14:21.549
That Reservoir Dogs wasn't his first movie, but he directed a very low-budget movie and he said he got all of his mistakes out of his.
《落水狗》并不是他的第一部电影，但他导演过一部预算极低的电影，他说他把所有的错误都在那部片里犯光了。

00:14:21.549 --> 00:14:23.789
So he just made tons of mistakes.
所以他犯了成吨的错误。

00:14:23.789 --> 00:14:29.470
And by the time he got to Reservoir Dogs, he had enough wherewithal to know how to delegate and figure it out.
等到他拍《落水狗》的时候，他已经有了足够的经验和头脑去懂得如何授权和解决问题。

00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:34.190
So he avoided a lot of the potholes that he fell into the first movie.
所以他避开了他在第一部电影中踩过的许多大坑。

00:14:34.190 --> 00:14:36.990
But you've got to go out and get your mistakes in.
但你必须亲自去把错误都犯一遍。

00:14:36.990 --> 00:14:37.830
Yeah.
是的。

00:14:37.830 --> 00:14:38.669
You have to.
你必须这么做。

00:14:38.669 --> 00:14:40.809
you'll learn so much from just doing.
你从实践中能学到太多东西。

00:14:40.809 --> 00:14:52.129
Yeah, and also I think the size of the movie or the TV show, it feels a little, you know, you see that there's a, I mean, how I met your mother, I had 120 people or whatever it was that made that thing.
是的，而且我觉得电影或电视剧的规模，感觉有点，你知道的，你看到有一个，我是说，《老爸老妈浪漫史》，我有120个人或者无论多少人共同打造了那个东西。

00:14:52.129 --> 00:14:55.210
And you watch the credits of your average movie.
你看普通电影的演职员表。

00:14:55.210 --> 00:14:57.250
It just goes on and on and on.
就是没完没了地滚动。

00:14:57.250 --> 00:15:03.049
And you feel like, oh, well, I only had like three guys help me make my little thing, so it's not real.
你会觉得，哦，好吧，我只有三个人帮我做我的小东西，所以它不是真的。

00:15:03.049 --> 00:15:04.730
But you just gotta get over that.
但你必须要克服这种心态。

00:15:04.730 --> 00:15:07.730
And something that I just finished making, just finished post production.
我最近刚做完的一部作品，刚刚完成后期制作。

00:15:07.730 --> 00:15:11.529
In the credits, I wrote the 11 people who made this movie.
在职员表里，我写上了制作这部电影的11个人的名字。

00:15:11.529 --> 00:15:17.169
And then there's the credits that run for about seven seconds, and you have a quick list of people that did it.
然后演职员表只滚动大约七秒钟，上面快速列出了参与制作的人员名单。

00:15:17.169 --> 00:15:21.690
And even with me, I have to get over the feeling of like, so is it a real movie?
即使是我，我也得克服那种感觉，比如：这真的是一部电影吗？

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:22.610
Is it a real movie?
这真的是一部电影吗？

00:15:22.610 --> 00:15:25.529
