我们不会占用你太多时间的。

00:34:13.059 --> 00:34:18.940
But the question was, what is it like when people praise you, praise me where the show are you?
但问题是，当人们赞美你、赞美我和这部剧时，那是一种什么样的体验？

00:34:18.940 --> 00:34:19.940
Can you take that?
你能接受吗？

00:34:19.940 --> 00:34:22.980
can move ahead, and how has that changed over your life?
可以继续，这随着你的生活发生了怎样的变化？

00:34:22.980 --> 00:34:25.980
Cause I know it's very different in your twenties and thirties than in the forties and thirties.
因为我知道你在二十多岁和三十多岁时的感受，跟四十多岁时是非常不同的。

00:34:25.980 --> 00:34:28.460
That's such a great, thoughtful question.
这是一个非常棒、很有深度的问题。

00:34:29.900 --> 00:34:55.079
You know, sometimes it's really hard to, except praise, like, I, how I met your mother, Jordana and my wife pointed out that when people come up to me and want to talk about how I met your mother, because we've been together four years and she said, since this podcast has been on, there's been a notable shift in how warm you are to how I met your mother fans who come up and want to talk to you about the show because I think I understand their enthusiasm more.
你知道的，有时候真的很难接受赞美，就像……《老爸老妈浪漫史》，乔丹娜和我的妻子指出，当人们走过来想跟我聊《老爸老妈浪漫史》时——因为我们已经在一起四年了，她说自从这个播客开播以来，我对那些走过来想找我聊这部剧的《老爸老妈浪漫史》粉丝的态度有了一个明显的转变，变得温暖多了，因为我觉得我更能理解他们的热情了。

00:34:55.079 --> 00:35:04.079
And it's like I've become a fan too, so I can share it more, more than feeling like I'm being kind of pinned against the wall or made to be some sort of zoo animal or something.
这就好像我也成了一个粉丝，所以我可以更多地去分享这份热情，而不是觉得像被逼到墙角或者被当成某种动物园里的动物一样。

00:35:04.079 --> 00:35:08.239
But so that's really been helpful.
所以这真的很有帮助。

00:35:08.239 --> 00:35:20.000
But my relationship to praise has gone through a lot of changes because I'm from the Midwest and I know people in Australia kind of deal with this where it's like, don't brag, don't act like you're better than anyone else.
不过我和赞美之间的关系经历了很多变化，因为我来自中西部，我知道在澳大利亚的人也有这种感觉，那就是：不要吹牛，不要表现得自己比任何人都优秀。

00:35:20.000 --> 00:35:22.820
So I was very self-effacing the word.
所以我以前总是非常谦逊，就是那个词。

00:35:22.820 --> 00:35:24.920
Like I was very, I would dodge compliments.
我以前总是会躲避赞美。

00:35:24.920 --> 00:35:33.820
I knew, but I was also like starving for external validation and wanting people to tell me I was good and talented and charming and wonderful.
我知道，但与此同时我也极度渴望外界的认可，希望别人告诉我我很优秀、很有才华、很有魅力、非常棒。

00:35:34.920 --> 00:35:36.800
But I really struggled with it.
但我真的很挣扎。

00:35:36.800 --> 00:36:00.360
And I had a very wise mentor figure who told me I needed to get over that and I needed to accept that I was good and talented and that if I didn't take an honest assessment of my own gifts, I wouldn't get where I needed to be in this life and this business, because he said every time he would compliment me, I would kind of run away.
我曾有一位非常明智的导师人物，他告诉我，我必须克服这一点，必须接受自己确实很优秀、很有才华，如果我不对自己的天赋做出诚实的评估，我就无法在这个生活和这个行业中达到我应有的高度，因为他说每次他夸我的时候，我都会像逃跑一样。

00:36:00.360 --> 00:36:02.280
I would dodge them, I wouldn't take it.
我会躲开赞美，不去接受它。

00:36:02.280 --> 00:36:16.860
So I think there's an art to accepting a compliment, because essentially when someone says, your work really moved me, or I really like that thing you made, If you say no, no, no, no, or run away or swat it away, you're actually telling them they have bad taste.
所以我认为接受赞美也是一门艺术，因为本质上当别人说“你的作品真的打动了我”或者“我真的很喜欢你做的那个东西”时，如果你说“不不不不”或者逃跑、把赞美推开，你实际上是在告诉他们他们的品味很差。

00:36:16.860 --> 00:36:22.659
Like you're being cruel to someone who is extending themselves and being kind.
这就好比你在对一个向你敞开心扉、释放善意的人表现得很刻薄。

00:36:22.659 --> 00:36:32.500
So I really try to work at being a gracious acceptor of compliments because I believe most people are sincere when they're saying something.
所以我真的很努力地让自己成为一个优雅地接受赞美的人，因为我相信大多数人在说某些话时都是真诚的。

00:36:32.500 --> 00:36:33.739
Right, right.
对，对。

00:36:33.739 --> 00:36:42.659
Yeah, I felt in something that I worked on, I feel the same way of just like, sure, of course you want people to like it and by extension, there's something about liking you.
是的，我在自己参与过的一些作品中也有同感，我也有同样的感受，就是：当然，你希望人们喜欢它，由此延伸开来，这也关乎到人们是否喜欢你。

00:36:42.659 --> 00:36:54.780
And the, I did this film, and when people would come up to me afterwards, the speed with which I would deflect to, oh yeah, we did this.
我拍过一部电影，当人们事后来找我时，我转移话题的速度简直快得惊人：“哦对，我们大家一起做的。”

00:36:54.780 --> 00:36:56.780
Oh yeah, the cast did this.
“哦对，演员们一起完成的。”

00:36:56.780 --> 00:36:57.659
The group did this.
“团队一起做的。”

00:36:57.659 --> 00:37:00.420
Just how fast can I get it away from me?
我能多快把功劳从自己身上撇开，就有多快。

00:37:00.420 --> 00:37:02.059
Couldn't be faster.
绝对没有比这更快的了。

00:37:02.059 --> 00:37:07.099
But of course, the person saying the tune, I think about myself, I don't really go up to too many people and say things.
但当然，说赞美之词的那个人……想想我自己，我其实不会主动去找太多人说那些话。

00:37:07.099 --> 00:37:09.099
I got, I picked very carefully.
我……我挑得非常仔细。

00:37:09.099 --> 00:37:11.820
I think complimented me in a while, Alec.
亚历克斯，我好久没听到别人夸我了。

00:37:11.820 --> 00:37:13.579
It's in my head every day.
这句话每天都在我脑子里打转。

00:37:13.579 --> 00:37:16.980
Yeah, I'd love to hear what you have to say.
对，我很想听听你要对我说什么。

00:37:16.980 --> 00:37:17.900
