I don't wanna do it.
我不想公开来。

00:37:19.579 --> 00:37:20.420
I'll be doing it.
我这就去私下说。

00:37:20.420 --> 00:37:22.579
I'll email you.
我会发邮件给你。

00:37:23.480 --> 00:37:37.989
But for a lot of people, also, the strength, the work, the preparation it takes to come up to someone and say, I loved you, I loved your work, is that takes a lot, I know we, yeah.
但对许多人来说，鼓起勇气走到一个人面前说“我喜欢你，我喜欢你的作品”，所需要的力量、努力和心理准备——这真的不容易，我知道我们，是的。

00:37:37.989 --> 00:37:48.869
Well, I would also say for the person who asked, how do you become, how do you break into the business from the East Coast, if someone's work moves you, write them a fan letter, reach out to them.
嗯，我也想对那个提问的人说，你是怎么进入这个行业的，怎么从东海岸打入这个圈子的？如果某个人的作品打动了你，就写一封粉丝信给他，去联系他。

00:37:48.869 --> 00:38:01.030
I've written fan letter, I mean, I'm in an advantaged position because people often know who I am, so it's like I can strike up an artistic kind of friendship kind of quickly by reaching out.
我写过粉丝信，我的意思是，我处于一个比较有利的位置，因为人们通常知道我是谁，所以通过主动联系，我能比较快地建立起一种艺术上的友谊。

00:38:01.030 --> 00:38:08.610
But I genuinely like, when I love something, like that reminds me, we watched Chris Fleming's Stand up special on HBO last night.
但我真心觉得，当我喜欢某样东西时——这让我想起，我们昨晚在HBO上看克里斯·弗莱明的单口喜剧专场。

00:38:08.610 --> 00:38:16.849
If you haven't seen it, it is one of the strangest wild, like he's such a visionary, strange alien of a stand up comedian.
如果你还没看过，那绝对是最古怪、最疯狂的节目之一，他就像是一个充满远见又怪异的单口喜剧外星人。

00:38:16.849 --> 00:38:17.690
Yeah.
是的。

